# short-description: Ozark OS SD card for the Raspberry Pi, with A/B system slots
# long-description: GPT (the Pi 4 boots from GPT), five partitions:
#   1 boot       firmware at the top; each slot's kernel, dtbs and config in a/ and b/
#   2 root       system slot A
#   3 rootb      system slot B: empty until the first update writes it
#   4 OZARKLOGS  plain-text boot logs (ozark-logs) that any PC can read. Separate
#                from boot so a power cut mid-write can only damage logs.
#   5 ozarkdata  settings, pairings and Dash's files (ozark-data): kept across
#                updates. Grows to fill the card on first boot.
# Slot sizes: OZARK_SLOT_SIZE (classes/ozark-slots.bbclass), 2560 MiB. All of it
# fits an 8 GB card. No mountpoints here (wic would add fstab lines):
# ozark-update (/boot), ozark-logs and ozark-data add them.

bootloader --ptable gpt
part --source bootimg-partition --ondisk mmcblk0 --fstype=vfat --label boot --active --align 4096 --size 256
part / --source rootfs --ondisk mmcblk0 --fstype=ext4 --label root --align 4096 --fixed-size ${OZARK_SLOT_SIZE}M
part --ondisk mmcblk0 --fstype=ext4 --label rootb --align 4096 --fixed-size ${OZARK_SLOT_SIZE}M
part --ondisk mmcblk0 --fstype=vfat --label OZARKLOGS --align 4096 --size 256
part --ondisk mmcblk0 --fstype=ext4 --label ozarkdata --align 4096 --size 256
